    "class": "unspecified",
    "evidence": "Fig. 5.68 'General plan of the structural remains in Central Area (1:500)' (PDF p. 111, printed p. 97) has no north arrow. Its base map, with the same contours and 5 m trench grid, is Fig. 3.2 'Trench numbers of the Central Area' (PDF p. 36). The report states on PDF p. 34 (printed p. 20): 'All the trenches in the main habitation area were oriented in cardinal directions (Figures 3.1 and 3.2).' Fig. 3.1 (PDF p. 35) shows the same 5 m grid with a four-point compass star marked 'N' drawn parallel to the grid. North is therefore taken as the page-upward direction of the grid's north-south lines; whether the cardinal directions are true or magnetic is not stated. The north line picked is the grid line at x 531, from south (bottom) to north (top).",
